# GitHub reads this for its "Cite this repository" button, Zenodo when it
# archives a release. It cites the explorer; the engine and EXIOBASE have
# their own citations (see README.md and docs/precompute.md).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: "RaMa-Scene Explorer"
abstract: >-
  RaMa-Scene Explorer traces the supply chains behind consumption using
  EXIOBASE v3.3.sm data for 2011. It maps where greenhouse-gas emissions,
  employment and metal-ore extraction occur across 49 countries and regions,
  grouped into 15 industry sections. Readers can trace a footprint, inspect
  its flows and compare 155 published scenarios. Custom scenarios can run in
  the browser or through an optional RaMa-Scene job API. The model changes
  monetary final demand or inputs per unit of output, with prices and other
  coefficients fixed. The results describe the 2011 economy, not forecasts.
  Methods, assumptions, provenance and numerical checks accompany the results.
  The code is MIT-licensed; derived EXIOBASE data is shared under CC BY 4.0.
version: 0.5.0
